{"title":"Policy Researcher Roadmap","role":"Policy Researcher","summary":"A Policy Researcher specializing in Human Rights Law studies laws, public policies, government programs, judicial decisions, and social issues to develop evidence-based recommendations for improving human-rights outcomes.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Human Rights Law"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Policy Researcher specializing in Human Rights Law studies laws, public policies, government programs, judicial decisions, and social issues to develop evidence-based recommendations for improving human-rights outcomes."},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law","Public Policy","Research","Data","Human Rights","Governance"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Policy Researchers may work with think tanks, NGOs, research organizations, universities, government programs, international organizations, consulting firms, advocacy organizations, and public-policy teams."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Policy Researcher” is not generally a regulated professional title. An LLB provides a strong legal foundation, but strong research, public-policy, economics, statistics, writing, and field-research capabilities significantly improve employability."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Typical Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Human Rights Policy"},{"text":"Researching rights-related policies and their outcomes"}],[{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Evaluating laws and government programs"}],[{"text":"Legal Policy Research"},{"text":"Studying legislation, judgments and regulatory frameworks"}],[{"text":"Social Policy"},{"text":"Researching education, health, poverty, gender and social protection"}],[{"text":"Governance Research"},{"text":"Studying institutions, administration and accountability"}],[{"text":"Constitutional Policy"},{"text":"Fundamental rights, constitutional governance and state action"}],[{"text":"International Human Rights"},{"text":"UN mechanisms, treaties and international standards"}],[{"text":"Labour & Social Justice"},{"text":"Labour rights, workplace policy and social protection"}],[{"text":"Child Rights"},{"text":"Child protection, education and welfare policy"}],[{"text":"Gender Policy"},{"text":"Gender equality, safety and inclusion"}],[{"text":"Migration & Refugee Policy"},{"text":"Migration, displacement and protection frameworks"}],[{"text":"Digital Rights"},{"text":"Privacy, AI, surveillance and freedom of expression"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["LLB / Integrated LLB","Human Rights Law Foundation","Legal Research + Public Policy","Research Internship","Policy Writing + Data Analysis","Research Assistant / Junior Policy Researcher","Policy Researcher","Senior Policy Researcher","Policy Lead / Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Advisor / Research Director"]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build the Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Legal Methods"},{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Legal Writing"},{"text":"Political Science"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Economics fundamentals"},{"text":"Human rights concepts"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Critical thinking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand key concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human dignity"},{"text":"Equality"},{"text":"Liberty"},{"text":"Non-discrimination"},{"text":"Rule of law"},{"text":"Access to justice"},{"text":"Social justice"},{"text":"Constitutional rights"},{"text":"State accountability"},{"text":"Vulnerable communities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Activities"},{"type":