text":"This framework can be used for topics such as education, healthcare, disability rights, gender equality, labour rights, digital rights and access to justice."}]},{"heading":"Important Indian Legal & Policy Areas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Human Rights Policy Researcher should become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitution of India"},{"text":"Fundamental Rights"},{"text":"Directive Principles of State Policy"},{"text":"Human-rights protection framework"},{"text":"Criminal justice system"},{"text":"Child protection framework"},{"text":"Women's rights framework"},{"text":"Labour and social-security laws"},{"text":"Disability rights"},{"text":"Data protection and privacy"},{"text":"Anti-discrimination principles"},{"text":"Access-to-justice mechanisms"},{"text":"Social welfare programs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also understand the role of institutions such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"National Human Rights Commission"},{"text":"State Human Rights Commissions"},{"text":"Courts"},{"text":"Government ministries"},{"text":"Parliament and legislative committees"},{"text":"National commissions"},{"text":"State-level commissions"},{"text":"Local government institutions"}]}]},{"heading":"International Human Rights Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universal Declaration of Human Rights"},{"text":"International human-rights treaties"},{"text":"UN human-rights mechanisms"},{"text":"Sustainable Development Goals"},{"text":"International Labour Organization frameworks"},{"text":"International humanitarian principles"},{"text":"Comparative constitutional systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A policy researcher should understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["international standards","domestic law","government policy","implementation","actual outcomes"]}]},{"heading":"Data & Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p",